:: Journey [planned]
Scene 2 contract: humane first contact and independent travel/receiving fields reconstruct the late journey. No later recording is released just because a phone screen opened. This scene is not implemented in the new edition.

[[Physical visit to Aurelia->Aurelia]]

:: Aurelia [planned]
Scene 3 contract: actual recorder, retained exports, calibrated clock and receiving originals. Anonymous crossing and field limits remain separate from identification. Lawful delivery resolves Luca's work gap.

[[Archive enquiry->Archive]]

:: Archive [planned]
Scene 4 contract: Mara's working place, private permission, public use and independently retained duplicate complicate the emotional account. Earlier incomplete phone lines acquire context.

[[Request older source index->Workshop]]

:: Workshop [planned]
Scene 5 contract: real slate, catalogue and case controls at a radio bench recover W-12's older source. Targeted follow-up separately releases later phone originals and provider retry fields.

[[Test accounts in their own places->Accounts]]

:: Accounts [planned]
Scene 6 contract: source-supported conversations, bounded innocent omissions and actual residential coverage. A possible route is not a witnessed journey.

[[Return with recovered originals->Return Room]]

:: Return Room [planned]
Scene 7 contract: original object, label layering, clinical wording, reassurance and positive custody sources. Reject exact-time, speaker-identification and contact-dating overclaims. The matrix records all prerequisites.

[[Prepare consequential assertions->Preparation]]

:: Preparation [planned]
Scene 8 contract: supported assertions, reasonable alternative fact access and explained private/public handling choices. The late personal original recontextualizes ordinary early material.

[[Confrontation and aftermath->Closure]]

:: Closure [planned]
Scene 9 contract: factual closure does not require a confession or publication of private grief. Time for reactions and a final voluntary action is part of the scene.

